--TEST--
Core\Arr::replaceRange renumbers the whole result, where array_splice renumbers the integer keys and keeps the string ones
--ORACLE-DIVERGES--
This is the same ADR 0069 § 3 rule that `arr-slice-on-string-keys-diverges-from-array_slice` pins, on the member that substitutes rather than returns — but here it is not an option's default, because `replaceRange` has no `preserveKeys` at all and could not honestly offer one: the entries either side of the window and the ones spliced into it cannot all keep a key without colliding. `array_splice` resolves that by keeping the strings and renumbering the integers around them, so its result's keys depend on how many earlier entries were integer-keyed; Novis renumbers subject and replacement alike, and the result is always a list from "0".
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Render {
    public static function of(array<int> $a): string {
        var $out = "";
        foreach ($a as string $k => int $v) {
            $out = $out . $k . "=" . $v . ";";
        }
        return $out;
    }
}

array<int> $rep = [7, 8];

// No integer key at all: `array_splice` answers `x=1;0=7;1=8;w=4;`, which is a
// map whose two spliced entries are integer-keyed and now sit in the same
// array as two string-keyed ones. Novis's answer is a list.
array<int> $map = ["x" => 1, "y" => 2, "z" => 3, "w" => 4];
echo Render::of(Core\Arr::replaceRange($map, 1, 2, $rep)), "\n";

// Both kinds of key: `array_splice($mixed, 1, 1, $rep)` answers
// `0=1;1=7;2=8;3=3;b=4;` — everything renumbered except the trailing `b`, so
// one entry of five kept its key and the rest did not.
array<int> $mixed = ["5" => 1, "x" => 2, "9" => 3, "b" => 4];
echo Render::of(Core\Arr::replaceRange($mixed, 1, 1, $rep)), "\n";

// An empty window at the end is an append on both sides, and it diverges for
// the same reason rather than a new one: PHP's `0=1;x=2;1=3;b=4;2=7;3=8;`
// keeps the two strings where Novis's result is a list.
echo Render::of(Core\Arr::replaceRange($mixed, 4, 0, $rep)), "\n";
--EXPECT--
0=1;1=7;2=8;3=4;
0=1;1=7;2=8;3=3;4=4;
0=1;1=2;2=3;3=4;4=7;5=8;
